cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article."
title: "ACP-SME: Adaptive Cybersecurity Protector for SMEs (reference prototype)"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and reproduction package for ACP-SME, a
  metadata-driven, privacy-oriented decision-support prototype that tailors an
  SME cybersecurity profile across NIST CSF 2.0, ISO/IEC 27001:2022 and CIS
  Controls v8.1 under an explicit resource budget. Includes the Minimum
  Necessary Metadata Model and its local metadata guard, a typed capability
  crosswalk, the material-change detector, an exact resource-constrained
  selector, a hash-chained human-authorized profile ledger, and the seeded
  synthetic experiment reported in the article. All results are synthetic model
  output; they do not demonstrate real-world incident reduction, standards
  conformity or certification readiness.
